                <pb facs="0430" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2326: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-24T20:00:00-03:00">May 24, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Leticia agreement signed 6 o’clock this afternoon. Last act of Conference
                    was to address a plea to Bolivia and Paraguay to seek peaceful solution of Chaco
                        conflict.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d462-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
